Hi Sean / Andrew / Lianet,

Thanks for all your review and suggestions.

AS1, LM1, LM4: Change to add KIP-848 information when users give =
=E2=80=94verbose option.
=E2=80=94describe =E2=80=94verbose: shows group epoch and target =
assignment epoch.
=E2=80=94describe =E2=80=94members =E2=80=94verbose: shows above =
information, member epoch, and target assignment.

AS2: Change to use MEMBER-EPOCH to align with KIP-848 definition.

LM2: For classic group, it doesn=E2=80=99t have epoch, so I use Optional =
fields in ConsumerGroupDescription.
For share group, it relies on KIP-848. It must have epoch, so I use int =
fields in ShareGroupDescription.

LM3: Remove =E2=80=94state change. We can get group level information by =
=E2=80=94describe =E2=80=94verbose.

SQ1: Add LEADER-EPOCH when users give =E2=80=94describe =E2=80=94offsets =
=E2=80=94verbose.

Thanks.
PoAn

> On Nov 1, 2024, at 5:08=E2=80=AFAM, Lianet M. <lianetmr@gmail.com> =
wrote:
>=20
> Hello Frank, thanks for the KIP! A few comments:
>=20
> LM1. I strongly agree with Andrew's suggestion of moving this into a
> --verbose option. I expect someone would only attempt to make sense of =
the
> epochs while debugging an issue, not while trying to view the group or
> member's info. (Also member-epoch makes more sense to me, even more if =
we
> end up agreeing in a --verbose). Related to both issues, my take is =
that
> whoever is close to the protocol will expect member-epoch, whoever is =
not
> will probably won't even need to see the epochs at all.
>=20
> LM2. Why are the epochs defined as Optional (don't we expect to always =
have
> them? with 0 initially, defined on the broker side for the group ones, =
and
> client side for the member)
>=20
> LM3. Why is the KIP including the =E2=80=93state option in the =
proposed changes? (
> =
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=3D3279774=
11#KIP1099:Extendkafkaconsumergroupscommandlinetooltosupportnewconsumergro=
up---state
> ).
> I get that the output would change in that example, but it=E2=80=99s =
not because of
> any change to the =E2=80=93state option itself. It's because of the =
change proposed
> to the =E2=80=93described (required with the --state), and the changes =
to
> --describe are already explained above (seems confusing, got me =
looking for
> a change to the state filter which seemed unrelated).
>=20
> LM4. Group epoch and target assignment epoch are conceptually at the =
group
> level. vs member epoch that lands at a member level. So wonder if we =
should
> show them accordingly (ex. using the --verbose option)
>  =E2=80=93describe =E2=80=93verbose =3D> shows group epoch and target =
assignment epoch
>                =E2=80=93describe =E2=80=93members =E2=80=93verbose =3D> =
shows member epoch (along
> with group epoch and target assignment epoch)
>=20
> Thanks!
>=20
> Lianet
>=20
