Thanks for the KIP Bill. Very useful addition to be able to collect all 
metrics broker side.

The KIP proposes to add a new thread-level metric for the thread state 
similar to the existing client "state" metric. The KIP lacks the 
corresponding definition though -- it only list the three new GAUGE 
metrics, but not the new thread-level STRING metric. Can you add the 
missing row to the table?



> Note that the "Name" column is the MBean name.

Well, not really. Of course, all information is there, but the "Name" is 
not the MBean name. The MBean is a concatenation of tags; cf 
https://kafka.apache.org/documentation/#kafka_streams_client_monitoring 
-- the MBean name is the last column, eg:

     kafka.streams:type=stream-metrics,client-id=([-.\w]+)


-Matthias

