> {code}
> [https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/trunk/core/src/main/scala/kafka/coo=
rdinator/transaction/TransactionMarkerRequestCompletionHandler.scala#L100]
> ------
> It is a data partition side bug. The leader may return the response early=
 without all the producer ID included in the response.
> Consider the following 2 cases:
>  # We have 2 markers to append, one for producer-0, one for producer-1
>  # When we first process producer-0, it appends a marker to the __consume=
r_offset.
>  # The __consumer_offset append finishes very fast because the group coor=
dinator is no longer the leader. So the coordinator directly returns NOT_LE=
ADER_OR_FOLLOWER. In its callback, it calls the=C2=A0{{maybeComplete()}}=C2=
=A0for the first time, and because there is only one partition to append, i=
t is able to go further to call=C2=A0{{maybeSendResponseCallback()}}=C2=A0a=
nd decrement=C2=A0{{{}numAppends{}}}.
>  # Then it calls the replica manager append for nothing, in the callback,=
 it calls the=C2=A0{{maybeComplete()}}=C2=A0for the second time. This time,=
 it also decrements=C2=A0{{{}numAppends{}}}.
> =C2=A0
>  # We have 2 markers to append, one for producer-0, one for producer-1
>  # When we first process producer-0, it appends a marker to the __consume=
r_offset and a data topic foo.
>  # The 2 appends will be handled by group coordinator and replica manager=
 asynchronously.
>  # It can be a race that, both appends finishes together, then they can f=
ill the=C2=A0{{markerResults}}=C2=A0at the same time, then call the=C2=A0{{=
{}maybeComplete{}}}. Because the=C2=A0{{partitionsWithCompatibleMessageForm=
at.size =3D=3D markerResults.size}}=C2=A0condition is satisfied, both=C2=A0=
{{maybeComplete}}=C2=A0calls can go through to decrement the=C2=A0{{numAppe=
nds}}=C2=A0and cause a premature response.
> Remember, because we only have 2 markers, the initial value for=C2=A0{{nu=
mAppends}}=C2=A0is also 2. So in step 4, it is able to finish the request w=
ithout even processing producer-1. This will cause the producer-1 missing f=
rom the WriteTxnMarkers response.
> ----
> As a result, the txn coordinator will not update the txn state correctly =
though the markers may have been written in the data partitions. There is a=
n impact on the clients. the client believes the txn is completed but when =
it tries to send any request for the new transaction with the same transact=
ion ID, the request will fail with CONCURRENT_TRANSACTIONS.=C2=A0
> Note, this can only happen with the KIP-848 coordinator enabled.



