Gavin,

I would still like to pursue this for Kafka. While we don't need the remote
cache for our builds (we make do with the GitHub Actions Cache currently),
I think the Develocity remote build cache would still be useful for
speeding up local development. At least, I would like to be able to kick
the tires and evaluate if committers could benefit from it.

-David

On Sat, Nov 2, 2024 at 7:52=E2=80=AFAM Gavin McDonald <gmcdonald@apache.org=
> wrote:

> Hi All.
>
> An INFRA Jira ticket was opened back in January this year. [1]
>
> A cache node was created on 23rd January.
>
> After some back and forth and chasing up Infra eventually closed
> the ticket in April as the last comment from the project was 11th March.
>
> The cache node has not ever been used as far as I can tell and is using
> up resources. This email is notice that Infra will delete the cache node
> within 2 weeks assuming no progress is made to start using it in that
> time.
>
> Kind Regards
>
> Gavin (ASF Infra)
>
> [1] - https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/INFRA-25336
>


--=20
David Arthur

