Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-18005) Return metadata of sensitive config
 when describe config
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Luke Chen created KAFKA-18005:
---------------------------------

             Summary: Return metadata of sensitive config when describe con=
fig
                 Key: KAFKA-18005
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18005
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Luke Chen
            Assignee: Luke Chen


Currently, when describing config for a resource, we'll get `null` if the c=
onfig is a sensitive config, ex: "ssl.keystore.certificate.chain", "ssl.key=
store.password". And when describing configs with them it'll always return =
something like this:=20
{code:java}
> bin/kafka-configs.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --entity-type brok=
ers --entity-name 2 --describe
Dynamic configs for broker 2 are:
=C2=A0 listener.name.plantext.ssl.keystore.key=3Dnull sensitive=3Dtrue syno=
nyms=3D{DYNAMIC_BROKER_CONFIG:listener.name.plantext.ssl.keystore.key=3Dnul=
l} {code}
It would be great if the broker can return some metadata of these sensitive=
 configs, like last modified timestamp, to allow readers (ex: the operator)=
 to know if this is an outdated value.



