om>
wrote:

> Hi Kafka devs,  I have initiated KIP-1011 in which we have concluded that
> we will replace deprecated `alterConfigs` with `incrementalAlterConfigs` =
in
> command line tool `CommandConfig`.  In the design, if the server doesn=E2=
=80=99t
> support `incrementalAlterConfigs`, we would fallback to `alterConfigs` fo=
r pre-4.0
> client and directly fail for a post-4.0 client.
>
> The KIP-1011 document link:
> KIP-1011: Use incrementalAlterConfigs when updating broker configs by
