Hi David,=20
Thank you very much for pointing out this, we didn=E2=80=99t mention the =
deprecation period for this change, since the `incrementalAlterConfigs` =
api can achieve all the capabilities of `alterConfigs` api (though =
it=E2=80=99s a best-effort approach, currently it=E2=80=99s 100% =
achievable in practice), which means switch directly to =
`incrementalAlterConfigs` won't bring any problems.

For KIP-1011, it=E2=80=99s main focus is to resolve the bug of =
KAFKA-13788 <https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-13788> , there =
will always be a compatibility-break upgrade even without KIP-1011, so =
we shouldn=E2=80=99t care too much about it, failing to land KIP-1011 on =
release-3.8 means we didn=E2=80=99t fix the bug promptly rather than we =
didn=E2=80=99t maintain good compatibility for `ConfigCommand`, we can =
directly use `incrementalAlterConfigs` since we are already on =
release-4.0.

Luke, do you have any new ideas concerning this description.

--
Best,
Ziming


