Hi, Divij,

Thanks for the KIP.

For log.message.timestamp.after.max.ms, I agree that there seems to be no
good reason to set a future timestamp in a record. So, changing the default
to 1 hour makes sense.

For log.message.timestamp.before.max.ms, a common usage is to use CDC to
extract records from a database to Kafka. During bootstrap, it's possible
for Kafka to get records with much older timestamps. Changing the defaults
will break those use cases.

Jun


