We are experiencing data loss when Kafka Connect source connector fails to =
send data to Kafka topic after receiving a retriable exception from a schem=
a registry (when converting the record).

Kafka cluster & connect details:
 # Kafka Connect version: 3.8.1
 # Kafka Version 3.6.1
 # Cluster size: 16 brokers
 # Number of partitions in Kafka data topic: 32
 # Number of partitions in offsets topic:=C2=A0
 # Replication Factor: 4
 # Min In Sync Replicas: 2
 # Unclean leader election disabled
 # Uses Apicurio schema registry to convert to Avro
 # Uses default error tolerance i.e., None

Producer configs
 * acks =3D -1
 * max.in.flight.requests.per.connection =3D 1
 * batch.size =3D 524288

Our connector uses the offsets committed by Kafka Connect (does not have an=
y internal checkpointing/state storage).

Data loss is noticed on occasion when a timeout is received during the [con=
vertTransformedRecod|https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/3.8.1/connect/run=
time/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/connect/runtime/AbstractWorkerSourceTas=
k.java#L398] call. The timeout is from connecting to the schema registry fo=
r the schema. Full stack trace [here|https://gist.github.com/twthorn/5764b9=
dae2664ca72e71c1e6ebd4c792]

