Thanks for the great suggestion.

How about using =E2=80=9CisClassic=E2=80=9D?
The term like =E2=80=9CisLegacy=E2=80=9D may be equivocal in the future.
For example, if we have a newer version of consumer / share consumer, =
the meaning will be different for different cases.
If we use =E2=80=9CisClassic=E2=80=9D, for MemberDescription in =
ClassicGroupDescription, the value can be always =E2=80=9Ctrue=E2=80=9D.
In ConsumerGroupDescription, it=E2=80=99s =E2=80=9Ctrue=E2=80=9D when =
it=E2=80=99s a classic member.
In ShareGroupDescription, it=E2=80=99s always =E2=80=9Cfalse=E2=80=9D.

Thanks,
PoAn

