hi Giridar

It seems your use case involves random reads, and you expect the consumer to =
return 1000 records from server at once. Therefore, you could increase the wa=
it time (fetch.max.wait.ms) and fetch size (fetch.min.bytes) to receive a lar=
ger response with as many records as possible.

A suitable value for fetch.min.bytes might be 'average size of records * 1000=
'. You may also need to increase max.partition.fetch.bytes. For fetch.max.wai=
t.ms, a value of 1500 ms might match your expectations.

Best,
Chia-Ping


