The =E2=80=9CisClassic=E2=80=9D field in ConsumerGroupDescribeResponse =
is a boolean value, so we can=E2=80=99t use it as the protocol string.
I change the =E2=80=9CPROTOCOL=E2=80=9D column to =E2=80=9CIS-CLASSIC=E2=80=
=9D in kafka-consumer-groups.sh.
It returns =E2=80=9Ctrue=E2=80=9D if a member is in a classic group or =
it=E2=80=99s a classic member in a consumer group.
In other cases, it returns =E2=80=9Cfalse=E2=80=9D.

I have a draft implementation in =
https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/17872.

