Lianet Magrans created KAFKA-18096:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: Allow new consumer to join group after subscribe to p=
attern if no matching topics
                 Key: KAFKA-18096
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18096
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: clients, consumer
            Reporter: Lianet Magrans
            Assignee: Lianet Magrans
             Fix For: 4.0.0


Currently the new consumer won't transition to joining after a call to subs=
cribe with Pattern if there are no matching topics. This was because the co=
ordinator does not allow to join without topics (or regex). If that validat=
ion is removed from the broker with KAFKA-18095, we should update the consu=
mer so that it attempts to join in that case.

=C2=A0

This should allow to enable this test for the new consumer https://github.c=
om/apache/kafka/blob/866d66229da658a5eb1fcb9da28624dd8d2f3e2a/core/src/test=
/scala/integration/kafka/api/AuthorizerIntegrationTest.scala#L1053



