Qiheng He created KAFKA-18103:
---------------------------------

             Summary: Kafka's Confluence Wiki appears to reference the wron=
g Hive integration site
                 Key: KAFKA-18103
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-18103
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Qiheng He


* When I looked at [https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/pages/viewpage.acti=
on?pageId=3D30747974#Ecosystem-SearchandQuery] , I noticed that the Kafka d=
ocumentation referenced [https://hiveka.weebly.com/] .
 *=20
{code:java}
Search and Query

Elasticsearch=C2=A0-=C2=A0This project, Kafka Standalone Consumer will read=
 the messages from Kafka, processes and index them in Elasticsearch. There =
are also several=C2=A0Kafka Connect connectors for Elasticsearch.

Presto=C2=A0- The Presto Kafka connector allows you to query Kafka in SQL u=
sing Presto.

Hive=C2=A0- Hive SerDe that allows querying Kafka (Avro only for now) using=
 Hive SQL {code}

 * This seems odd, since Hive support for Kafka is directly at [https://git=
hub.com/apache/hive/blob/master/kafka-handler/README.md] .
- Is it a typo that the Confluence Wiki for Kafka references HiveKa at [htt=
ps://hiveka.weebly.com/] ? Or did the two merge at some point in time?



